meta {
  name: 26-Submit my first offer
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/offers
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{temi_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "listingId": 1,
    "amount": 780000,
    "currency": "NGN",
    "message": "Hi! I came for the inspection on Saturday and I love the place. ₦780,000 is what I can do for the year — I have 1 year up front ready to transfer. Please let me know."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: in [201, 400, 401, 403, 404, 409]
}

docs {
  After the inspection IRL on Saturday I'm offering ₦780,000 — a
  bit below the asking ₦850k because that's still on the high end
  for a self-con in Yaba (₦700k–₦900k is the market band per my
  research).

  No fields for "move-in date", "lease length", or "any conditions
  (landlord must repaint)". Just amount + free-text message. So
  every meaningful term has to live in `message` — and the owner
  has to manually parse it. As a real renter I'd expect structured
  fields for at least move-in date and lease length.

  Also: the spec says I can only have one PENDING offer per
  listing — so if I get the amount wrong here I have to wait for
  the owner to decline or I have to counter myself. There's no
  edit / withdraw on `/offers/{id}`.
}
